DFlash2 drafts for Flash Next (incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2) instead of the MTP head, on the concurrent
(--parallel >= 2) one-GPU engine. Drafts only change speed: every draft is verified by the target.
- cuda/dflash2.py (new): the drafter (5 layers, block 8, top-16 candidates a position, selector chain), reusing GLM's
  DFlash2 port (glm5_next/cuda/dflash2.py: prep kernel, chain rule, 4-bit linears). A 2,176-row context ring per stream
  slot; every round's context rows and draft blocks of all drafting streams run as one batched pass each (CUDA graphs:
  tap passes of 8..64 rows, block passes of 1..PARALLEL streams; 9 streams: drafting 21.5 -> 5.4 ms a round). A context
  starts at a resumed prompt's resume point (keys before it masked). Logits over Flash Next's draft vocabulary (the EXL3
  head's rows requantized to 4 bits); TENSORFOLD_DFLASH_VOCAB=full scores the whole head.
- forward.py: the taps are the mean of the 4 hyper-connection streams after target layers 5/15/25/35/45 (as the
  checkpoint's SGLang capture patch), read right after the next layer's write-back; the target's arithmetic is unchanged.
- multi.py, multi_fill.py: each round's committed rows feed their stream's context, prompt passes feed the prompt's last
  window, drafts follow each round and each prompt end. The lone-stream graph slot stays MTP-only (EXL3 verify is
  GPU-bound: graphs did not speed one stream up, and moving a stream into the slot slowed later requests).
- engine.py, __init__.py: --drafter DIR (a DFlash2 checkpoint) loads no MTP head and counts the drafter (weights, head,
  rings) in the startup estimate; --mtp-drafts (default 7) and --mtp-confidence (default 0.5, swept 0.15/0.3/0.5/0.7)
  set the drafts a round and the floor of a chain's probability product.
- TENSORFOLD_DFLASH_TIMING=1 prints the mean verify and drafting ms every 50 rounds (synchronizes; for profiling).
Needs 0005 (same functions). Off: DRAFTER=none (MTP as in flash-2; start.sh then leaves this patch out).
Verified on a GB10 (0.6.6, 4.05bpw_h6_ng6): greedy drafted replies equal "draft": false byte for byte, including a
16,993-token prompt, a resumed chat turn and an image prompt; 4 concurrent drafted replies equal each alone undrafted;
greedy suite (1/4/9 clients) accepted 79% / 73% / 84% / 57% of drafts (code / DevOps / JSON / prose), 4.7 / 4.1 / 6.0 /
2.1 tokens a round.

